Port patch 0014 - give the Area Select magnemite trails room for their six afterimages
Why: AreaSelect_AdvanceMagnemiteTrail writes six afterimages per trail although the struct declares four (a deliberate decomp trick:
"FAKE" note in area_select.c), so the last of the three trails writes 0xC bytes past the end of sAreaSelectMagnemiteTrails[3]. The
original compiler's layout of these statics is not known here (presumably the spill was harmless); on the native build the compiler orders the statics differently and the spill overwrote
sAreaSelectSelectedIndex (became 0x135), the banner texture lookup went far out of range and the renderer crashed (found by running
the game, located with a data watchpoint). The array gets two spare elements; nothing else changes.

--- a/src/fragments/area_select/area_select.c
+++ b/src/fragments/area_select/area_select.c
@@ -119,7 sha256=60a694bdaa05cbbc439db7b3746b8ad423504c1f14bd9163f76a6200487b40a4 @@
=3
-1
+/* PORT: 5 elements instead of 3. The code addresses six afterimages per trail (see the FAKE note on the struct), so the last trail's
+ * writes reach 0xC bytes past the end of the three-element array (offset 0x78 of 0x6C). The original compiler's layout of these statics is not known here (it was presumably harmless);
+ * on the port the compiler lays the statics out differently and it overwrote sAreaSelectSelectedIndex (found by running the game: the
+ * area index became 0x135 and the banner texture lookup read far outside its table). The two extra elements are only room for the spill. */
+static AreaSelectMagnemiteTrail sAreaSelectMagnemiteTrails[5];
=3
